{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"301","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Yaroslav and Algorithm"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yaroslav likes algorithms. We'll describe one of his favorite algorithms."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The algorithm receives a string as the input. We denote this input string as "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The algorithm consists of some number of command. Сommand number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" looks either as "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"si"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":">>"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"wi"},{"kind":"text","text":", or as "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"si"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"<>"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"wi"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"si"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"wi"},{"kind":"text","text":" are some possibly empty strings of length at most "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"7"},{"kind":"text","text":", consisting of digits and characters \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" At each iteration, the algorithm looks for a command with the minimum index "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":", such that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"si"},{"kind":"text","text":" occurs in "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" as a substring. If this command is not found the algorithm terminates. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Let's denote the number of the found command as "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":". In string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" the first occurrence of the string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"sk"},{"kind":"text","text":" is replaced by string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"wk"},{"kind":"text","text":". If the found command at that had form "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"sk"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":">>"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"wk"},{"kind":"text","text":", then the algorithm continues its execution and proceeds to the next iteration. Otherwise, the algorithm terminates. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The value of string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" after algorithm termination is considered to be the output of the algorithm. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yaroslav has a set of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" positive integers, he needs to come up with his favorite algorithm that will increase each of the given numbers by one. More formally, if we consider each number as a string representing the decimal representation of the number, then being run on each of these strings separately, the algorithm should receive the output string that is a recording of the corresponding number increased by one."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Help Yaroslav."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ n ≤ 100)"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the number of elements in the set. The next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contains one positive integer each. All the given numbers are less than "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1025"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the algorithm which can individually increase each number of the set. In the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th line print the command number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" without spaces."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your algorithm will be launched for each of these numbers. The answer will be considered correct if:   "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Each line will a correct algorithm command (see the description in the problem statement). "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The number of commands should not exceed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"50"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The algorithm will increase each of the given numbers by one. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" To get a respond, the algorithm will perform no more than "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"200"},{"kind":"text","text":" iterations for each number. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"